\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Sharing AOT code through per-runtime Runtime Indirection Tables (RITs). Instead of generating an interpreter for each runtime, \unhbox \voidb@x {\sc  AmberMonkey}{} shares one interpreter and $K$ CacheIR stub bodies across $N$ runtimes. Shared code loads the RIT base from the current frame (1), then retrieves the runtime's pointer from its table (2).}}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rit-access}{{3}{5}{Sharing AOT code through per-runtime Runtime Indirection Tables (RITs). Instead of generating an interpreter for each runtime, \AM {} shares one interpreter and $K$ CacheIR stub bodies across $N$ runtimes. Shared code loads the RIT base from the current frame (1), then retrieves the runtime's pointer from its table (2)}{figure.caption.5}{}}
